From: edde746 <86283021+edde746@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] player: let the first video frame out before the audio output opens

Opening an audio output is synchronous on the core thread, and
fill_audio_out_buffers() does it as soon as the audio filters know their
format, which is before write_video() looks at the first decoded frame:
run_playloop() calls them in that order. So the frame, decoded and
waiting, is shown only after the output is open, although audio cannot
start before that frame has given it a timestamp to sync to
(get_sync_pts() waits for video_status >= STATUS_READY).

On iOS the wait is long: ao_avfoundation's init takes 7 ms when the app
has already activated its audio session and 42 ms when it has to
activate it (26 ms once it has been active before), all of it on the
core thread, and a route that has to wake up takes longer still. An
iPhone's log of a second load: frame decoded at +36 ms, "Trying audio
driver 'avfoundation'" at +37, AO open at +72, frame shown at +77.

While a file starts with a video track whose first frame has not been
queued, and no audio output is open, leave the output closed;
run_playloop() comes back for it as soon as write_video() has queued the
frame (or the video chain ended, failed or turned out sparse). The
restart itself is where it was: the same work, in another order.

In series.apple only. Where the video decoder runs on its own thread
(--vd-queue-enable, as Plezy sets on Android) the output used to open
while the decoder worked, and waiting for the frame would add the open
to the restart there; that needs its own measurement.

iPhone Air, ms after loadfile until AVSampleBufferDisplayLayer reports
its first frame ready (1 kHz poll), medians of 3 interleaved runs,
Plezy's / Tortuga's option set, before -> after:
  H.264 1080p MP4, audio session activated by the AO
                                  89.4 -> 52.7 / 88.3 -> 51.5
  the same, session already active     48.5 -> 38.8 / 45.8 -> 39.8
  the same, second player in the process
                                  71.8 -> 37.1 / 72.7 -> 37.5
  HEVC 4K 90 Mb/s                121.0 -> 89.6 / 122.6 -> 87.1
  HEVC 1080p + ASS subtitles      86.0 -> 49.4 / 87.1 -> 49.9
PLAYBACK_RESTART for the same rows: 92.8 -> 92.9 / 90.2 -> 91.2,
48.9 -> 46.1 / 47.1 -> 46.8, 73.8 -> 75.0 / 74.3 -> 74.9,
124.1 -> 127.0 / 124.1 -> 125.3, 93.6 -> 97.7 / 89.0 -> 90.7.

diff --git a/player/audio.c b/player/audio.c
index e581066..565ada4 100644
--- a/player/audio.c
+++ b/player/audio.c
@@ -912,6 +912,22 @@ static void handle_ao_events(struct MPContext *mpctx)
     issue_refresh_seek(mpctx, MPSEEK_EXACT);
 }
 
+// Opening an audio output takes this thread tens of milliseconds, and far
+// longer where the route has to wake up first (activating an iOS audio
+// session, a Bluetooth route). While a file starts, a decoded first video
+// frame would sit behind that, although audio cannot start before the frame
+// has given it a timestamp to sync to (get_sync_pts). So the output opens
+// once that frame went to the VO; run_playloop() comes back for it.
+bool audio_output_waits_for_video(struct MPContext *mpctx)
+{
+    struct ao_chain *ao_c = mpctx->ao_chain;
+    return ao_c && ao_c->filter->ao_needs_update && !mpctx->ao &&
+           mpctx->opts->initial_audio_sync &&
+           mpctx->audio_status == STATUS_SYNCING &&
+           mpctx->vo_chain && !mpctx->vo_chain->is_sparse &&
+           mpctx->video_status == STATUS_SYNCING;
+}
+
 void fill_audio_out_buffers(struct MPContext *mpctx)
 {
     struct MPOpts *opts = mpctx->opts;
@@ -930,6 +946,8 @@ void fill_audio_out_buffers(struct MPContext *mpctx)
     }
 
     if (ao_c->filter->ao_needs_update) {
+        if (audio_output_waits_for_video(mpctx))
+            return;
         if (reinit_audio_filters_and_output(mpctx) < 0)
             return;
     }
diff --git a/player/core.h b/player/core.h
index c3e0816..ac01925 100644
--- a/player/core.h
+++ b/player/core.h
@@ -511,6 +511,7 @@ float audio_get_gain(struct MPContext *mpctx);
 void audio_update_volume(struct MPContext *mpctx);
 void reload_audio_output(struct MPContext *mpctx);
 void audio_start_ao(struct MPContext *mpctx);
+bool audio_output_waits_for_video(struct MPContext *mpctx);
 
 // configfiles.c
 void mp_parse_cfgfiles(struct MPContext *mpctx);
diff --git a/player/playloop.c b/player/playloop.c
index fa4bf44..50baad5 100644
--- a/player/playloop.c
+++ b/player/playloop.c
@@ -1279,8 +1279,12 @@ void run_playloop(struct MPContext *mpctx)
     if (mpctx->lavfi && mp_filter_has_failed(mpctx->lavfi))
         mpctx->stop_play = AT_END_OF_FILE;
 
+    bool ao_waited = audio_output_waits_for_video(mpctx);
     fill_audio_out_buffers(mpctx);
     write_video(mpctx);
+    // The audio output that let the first video frame go first.
+    if (ao_waited && !audio_output_waits_for_video(mpctx))
+        mp_wakeup_core(mpctx);
 
     handle_playback_restart(mpctx);
 
